# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Maruti Jal — environment template
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit .env or .env.local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# App runtime connection — MUST use the Neon POOLED host.
# The pooled host has "-pooler" in it, e.g.
#   ep-xxxx-pooler.c-3.ap-southeast-1.aws.neon.tech
# Using the direct host here exhausts Neon connections under serverless.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Migrations, migration:generate and seeds — MUST use the DIRECT (non-pooled) host.
# Same string as above, without "-pooler". DDL through PgBouncer is unreliable.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Connections per serverless instance. 3 is right behind PgBouncer; higher buys nothing.
DB_POOL_MAX=3

# Auth.js session secret. Generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=""

# Origin the server uses to call its OWN API from a Server Component.
#
# OPTIONAL, and normally left unset. On Vercel it is derived from
# VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL; locally it falls back to localhost:PORT.
# Set it only to pin a custom domain — and note it is a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var, so it
# is inlined at BUILD time: changing it needs a redeploy, not just a save.
#
# NEVER set this to a localhost address on Vercel. lib/api/client.ts ignores
# such a value deliberately, because honouring it makes every server-side fetch
# ECONNREFUSED, which surfaces as "signed out immediately after signing in".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="https://maruti-jal.vercel.app"

# NO DEFAULT_LOCALE, NO SEED_DEMO — both were documented here and read by
# nothing. The default language is `defaultLocale` in src/i18n/config.ts; demo
# data is `npm run db:seed:demo`. A variable nothing reads is worse than no
# variable, for the same reason TZ was dropped below.

# NO TZ VARIABLE — deliberately.
#
# Vercel reserves TZ and will not accept it, and this app does not need it. The
# process timezone is never consulted: `lib/dates.ts` names Asia/Kolkata in
# every Intl call, `todayIST()` derives the business date explicitly, and the
# four date-sensitive SQL views use `(now() AT TIME ZONE 'Asia/Kolkata')::date`.
#
# Setting `TZ=UTC` was belt-and-braces against a stray `new Date()` leaking the
# host zone into a stored date. The braces were never load-bearing, and Vercel's
# runtime is UTC regardless. Renaming it to TIME_ZONE would leave a variable
# nothing reads, which is worse than no variable at all.
#
# If this ever serves a second business in another zone, the change is
# `IST_TIMEZONE` in lib/dates.ts AND the four views — not an env var, because a
# view cannot read one.

# Log level: debug | info | warn | error
LOG_LEVEL="info"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On Vercel, only two of the above are actually required:
#   DATABASE_URL   (pooled host)
#   AUTH_SECRET
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED is read only by db/typeorm.config.ts — migrations and
# seeds, which run from a developer machine, never inside the deployed app.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
